(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ac-10"] = {"468337101":[["Wyatt","Any leads on the perpetrator's origin?"],["UNCS Captain","The GSA has some clues, but..."],["UNCS Captain","The Staff Department issued a notice four minutes ago, attributing the incident to the illegal crossing by the DLAF in external statements..."],["UNCS Captain","As for the real perpetrator... no team has been assigned to investigate yet."],["Wyatt","......"],["Wyatt","It's been fifteen years... Still playing this game..."],["","In the evil wind of dusk, the cowboy-dressed man sniffs his unlit cigarette, trying to use the tobacco scent to block the pervasive smell of burning and blood in the air."],["","Before him, the once indestructible steel wall has been melted into a large hole by an unknown weapon, scattered ST debris and charred bodies fused together, lying in various pits and craters."],["","This is a secret underground fortress within the Mouty Mountains region, which was used as a secret laboratory for human experimentation projects by the Predator forces during the Blair era."],["","After being taken over and sealed by the GSA, it has remained abandoned, with only a small number of Security Personnel guarding it."],["","All valuable assets within have either been transferred in advance or destroyed on site."],["","Apart from the basic infrastructure items that are neither useful nor easy to transfer, this old fortress is almost an empty city."],["","However, this old fortress, which has been sealed for years and holds no plunder value, was suddenly attacked the night before last..."],["Wyatt","The missing item is called the \"Vulcan Bracket,\" right?"],["Wyatt","The old-fashioned ST assembly bracket produced with metric specifications?"],["","Wyatt shifts his gaze to the melted opening and the two shocking drag marks outside."],["UNCS Captain","Yes... It was long obsolete, and its massive size made transportation costs too high. Even if we hauled it out, it would only be used for scrap..."],["UNCS Captain","Therefore, after completing the risk assessment, it was ultimately decided to leave it in the fortress for disposal..."],["Wyatt","...Was it really just scrap metal...? I remember in my time, this was quite valuable."],["UNCS Captain","Well... the staff department speculates that after the thief discovered the fortress was empty, they dismantled that old assembly frame as a consolation prize..."],["","Is that so? Just because they found nothing, they chose to dismantle the massive \"Vulcan Frame\" as compensation for a wasted trip?"],["","Or was that just way to cover up some other motive?"],["Wyatt","Submit a report to the GSA. I want a risk assessment and archival records from when the fortress was sealed..."],["Wyatt","By the way, check the production batch and installation information for this batch of \"Vulcan Frames.\""],["UNCS Captain","Got it!"],["","Wahhh—!!!"],["","A massive oilcloth cover crashes onto the dust-covered ground, echoing loudly within the mountain."],["","Amidst the stirred-up dust, two enormous gate-like frames can be faintly seen, along with scattered track networks and the load-bearing structures of the cave ceiling."],["","This is a mercenary base converted from an abandoned mine, where the weathered \"Vulcan Frame\" stands tall in the vast hollow of the mine's depths."],["Skysweep","Not too big, not too small, just right! You gotta hand it to them—those old-school engineers really cared about their craft."],["Skysweep","No extra tracks needed, no fresh equipment required, just connect the sliding base of the assembly rack with two regular minecart tracks!"],["Skysweep","Just prop up these iron gadgets... Hey, wherever you take them, it's an ST assembly plant!"],["","In the dim light, a slender figure wearing a line cap dances over to the minecart tracks under the rack, casually kicking the connecting structure and producing a thumping echo."],["","The girl busy behind the console lazily responds while humming a tune."],["Liliya","It can only handle some old models that have long been discontinued... The STs on Milkhama were originally built for mining, so aligning the assembly frame with the mine car tracks makes perfect sense."],["Liliya","As for later, those chaotic ST manufacturers got involved, and the specifications for the supporting equipment went haywire—hey!"],["","After adjusting several electronic valves, the girl suddenly pulls the main switch on the side of the wall, and the lighting equipment installed on the mine cave walls activates in sequence, neatly casting light toward the center of the cavity."],["","Meanwhile, the man with the wire cap standing at the base of the frame also activates a switch at the connection point, causing the pulleys at the base of the Vulcan Frame to emit bursts of noise..."],["","At the end of XC 119, after being sealed for nearly 20 years, the abandoned mine located at the southwest corner of Milkhama Island once again echoes with the roar of engines."],["","This ST workshop, constructed from mine car tracks, engineering machine engines, and retired Vulcan Frames, is now complete... just like the team within it, pieced together in a haphazard manner."],["Skysweep","Job done? Now we just wait for your boss to rescue that professor, and then we start assembling Liliya?"],["","Skysweep lightly brushes off the dust from his hands and turns to look at the Ovettian girl who is still busy."],["Liliya","That thing is not called Liliya, it's Leviathan, Le-vi-a-than! Liliya is MY name..."],["Liliya","And Goman doesn't really count as our boss—we're just working together for the time being..."],["Skysweep","So it's not a three-party deal anymore. What's it now, four? Five?"],["","Sacrificial pawn of the DLAF, traitor of the NDF, insider of the GSA, outcast army of Ovett... Of course, there's also himself, the one and only genius in the Thunderbolt Squad!"],["","Five individuals from different factions and backgrounds are tasked with using this pile of scattered equipment to restore the Mobile Fortress that attacked Milthus..."],["Skysweep","Listen, you guys aren't seriously planning to use that thing to crash into the governor's building in Rayneburg, are you...?"],["","The tone of Skysweep's voice unusually deepens. Even he thinks this idea is a bit too crazy..."],["Liliya","That's a question of how it's used. I don't care about that... What I care about is what's written in the Project 1099 file..."],["","Before Liliya can finish, a red light in the upper-left corner of the console suddenly begins to flash."],["","It's the emergency transmission indicator. The line was only completed early this morning, yet it's already seeing use."],["Liliya","Liliya speaking. Who's this...?"],["","Liliya picks up the receiver. Ragged breathing wheezes from the other end, like air escaping from a broken old bellows..."],["Liliya","Hello...?"],["","Liliya turns a dial on the console, trying to tune the signal, but all she gets from the other end is a blur of static."],["Liliya","Streetsweep..."],["Skysweep","It's Skysweep! Sky—sweep!"],["Liliya","Alright, Skysweep... Looks like your big friend is in trouble..."],["Wyatt","This is quite the welcoming ceremony... Since you're messing around on my turf, shouldn't you at least consult me, the host?"],["","An ST topples backward into the border desert's sandstorm, its chainsaw blade flashing in the sun."],["","Loose as a tumbleweed, the cowboy barrels through one enemy after another. Nothing's stopping him."],["","The GSA hasn't even decided whether to pursue the case, yet Wyatt Morgan has already embarked on a solo investigation."],["","Although the mastermind behind this theft remains unknown, the identity of the perpetrator can be roughly confirmed..."],["","Farlin, or her current name... Grimbite."],["Wyatt","Your codename... is Blazetrudge, right?"],["","Even though he is now surrounded, Wyatt's tone remains casual, as if he were just strolling along the seaside avenue in Milthus, accidentally crushing two fallen leaves..."],["Blazetrudge","Huff... huff..."],["","A wheezing sound like broken bellows emanates from the speaker, and amidst the swirling dust and sand, a Hannibal ST wielding a massive flamethrower stands before him."],["","As expected, it was likely him who melted the outer wall of the old fortress, and he also serves as the rear guard, intercepting all pursuers."],["Blazetrudge","Blazetrudge's mission... is to eliminate you..."],["","The dust and sand rise again, and scorching flames accompanied by several newly emerged red dots surge toward Wyatt."],["Wyatt","Tsk, in the end, it's all about who has the bigger fist... This broken island didn't disappoint me after all."],["","Wyatt pulls down the detection visor on the cockpit, and the blade wheel of the chainsaw starts spinning again..."]],"468337301":[["Heinz","The new group of mercenaries you found has retreated... I remember you said your ally would try to buy time within UNCS territory..."],["Heinz","Progress doesn't seem ideal, does it?"],["","Amidst the rumbling noise of chains and engines, the man half-made of machinery turns off the monitor installed on his prosthetic hand and glances at his long-haired collaborator."],["","On a towing platform nearby, the Ovettian who knows his pain all too well cuts the comm at his ear and turns to meet Heinz's gaze."],["","Yevgeny Ivanovic Goman—the notorious troublemaker both on and off the island—is now his ally."],["Yevgeny","...My informant has already filled me in about that wildcard. His name's Wyatt Morgan—he's off following those old leads, solo."],["Yevgeny","I remember you crossed paths with him during the last war... You haven't forgotten him, have you?"],["Heinz","Is it him... Has he returned to the NDF?"],["","Heinz instinctively shifts the mechanical half of his body. The face of one of the men responsible for it all flashes through his mind."],["Yevgeny","The old bastards at military command are getting restless. With Rosemary out of contact, they want to knock the bureaucrats down a peg..."],["Yevgeny","If they're sending him, they must be running low on attack dogs..."],["Yevgeny","Honestly, I wish I had your luck. People who have a grudge against you are always eager to stick their necks out for you to chop... Isn't this another great opportunity?"],["","Goman's voice carries a teasing edge. He glances at Heinz, waiting for a reaction."],["","Heinz doesn't take the bait. He only stares out at the gray-black sea, silent as a weathered statue."],["","At last, a dull boom rolls in from the nearby shore—the sound of something massive slamming into the seawall."],["","The towing platform is no longer moving smoothly. With the wreck's buoyancy gone, all eight tow cables pull taut under the strain."],["","The prize they've been dreaming of is almost ashore. Crews and machinery along the coast give one final heave, dragging the long-submerged corpse back into the light."],["","Under Port Kelvin's night sky, the salt-soaked wreck is hauled ashore. The rust-eaten \"1099\" on its flank bears witness to the years below."],["","The Mobile Fortress Leviathan, shot down from the high skies of Milthus, has returned to its creator."],["Yevgeny","It's even more wrecked than I imagined... Are you really confident you can restart this pile of scrap metal?"],["","Goman descends from thetraction platform and slowly walks to Heinz's side. Standing shoulder to shoulder, they gaze upwards."],["Heinz","Get your mercenaries ready... We don't have time to waste."],["Noisy communication","—Kzzzt—western outskirts of Thepia—kzzzt—sync first—"],["Noisy communication","—Ambush the prison convoy—kzzzt—morning of the 5th—kzzzt—"],["Noisy communication","————"],["","The transmission cuts off mid-sentence. Wyatt tears off the comm headset, and silence settles over the battered cockpit once more."],["","The mercenaries he drove off clearly have more pieces in play. They're coordinating across multiple locations, carrying out some unknown operation."],["","They knew someone would come after them. Worse, they pinpointed his position and laid a neat little ambush for the lone investigator..."],["","Without Fenrisúlfr, those mercs would've had him."],["Wyatt","Shame none of them made it... Otherwise, he'd know who's backing them."],["","Wyatt yanks out the comm cable and climbs from the wrecked enemy ST. In the morning light, he studies a map of Milkhama spread before him and lights a cigarette with practiced ease."],["","In the end, he closes the intercepted recording without sending it to military command or the GSA."],["","Not because he's desperate to play rebel, but because he suspects someone's already watching him."],["","There's no question: someone inside the GSA or military command is helping the other side."],["","That unseen mole is working with the mystery mercenaries, weaving a net meant to swallow all of Milkhama."],["","And now, Wyatt may have plucked one of its threads."],["","The spider won't be far behind, hungry for one lonely piece of prey."],["","Assuming, of course, this world has spiders big enough to swallow a giant, hulking ST."],["Harpy Broker","Hey, chips, cookies, peanuts—what takes ya fancy?"],["","A deep male voice suddenly comes through the line."],["","The cowboy blows a smoke ring, then grinds his cigarette out on a spot between Port Kelvin and Thepia, burning a tiny hole through the map."],["Wyatt","Silver Heart Tequila. Don't skimp on the ice."],["Harpy Broker","Well, look who it is. Missed your call earlier, buddy... What's up?"],["Wyatt","Got a job for you, old-timer. Can you patch me through to your boss, Miss Sand Whale?"],["Wyatt","There's something I need her to look into."]],"468341101":[["","Can anyone truly overcome regret?"],["DL Soldier","... The transport convoy is under attack! Requesting immediate support from the defense battalion! Requesting immediate support!"],["","Or is it fate that I must carry this burden for the rest of my life, barely hanging on?"],["DL Soldier","Those guys are Vesper!? That treacherous scum, choosing a time like this..."],["","However, whether or not these questions have an answer, it no longer matters..."],["DL Soldier","...Transfer all prisoners to Prisoner Transport No. 3! All other units provide full cover!"],["","Because everything is beyond redemption."],["DL Captain","Hey! I told you to get outta here? Are you even listening?!"],["DL Captain","What are you standing around for? Move it!"],["Ludwig","Sorry, sir, but my shackles haven't been removed."],["DL Captain","How could you have shackles, you're..."],["","The guard assigned to the transfer freezes. There really is a composite shackle around the prisoner's ankle, chained straight to the cell bars..."],["DL Captain","I remember you... You're the ST scientist who built Leviathan and bombed half the western district..."],["","The man in the corner says nothing. He only shifts his gaze, eerily calm."],["DL Captain","You, step forward a little—but not too close!"],["","The guard draws his sidearm, preparing to shoot and break the shackle bolt at the joint."],["","However, the man just stands there, motionless, staring at him."],["DL Captain","Don't waste my time. Didn't you hear what I said?"],["Ludwig","Sir, I'd like to ask you a favor... Can you just shoot me right here and finish me off?"],["DL Captain","Wh-What the hell are you talking about?"],["Ludwig","A grenade might look more like an accident... If I die in the chaos of an attack on the prison, no one will blame you..."],["","The string of requests leaves the transfer guard speechless."],["","He stares at the frail prisoner, as if checking whether he's nothing more than a corpse that learned to talk."],["","You're right, Lucas. I'm weak. Carrying this regret alone has worn me down..."],["DL Captain","You freakin' lunatic!"],["","Bang!"],["","Sparks fly. The bullet shears through the prisoner's shackle. The guard reaches for Ludwig's collar—then feels cold metal against the back of his head."],["","A cold gun barrel presses against his skull."],["DL Captain","Who—"],["","Bang!"],["","The guard collapses in a spray of blood. From the shadows behind him emerges a face—a visage locked in a fixed smile."],["Mirestomp","Nice to meet you, Professor Ludwig... Someone sent me to pick you up."],["Wyatt","You want me to stop the investigation... That's what this is about, right?"],["","Inside the cockpit, Wyatt leans back in the pilot's seat and stares at the comm window above."],["???","Still hesitating? If you need the reason again, I'll give it to you..."],["???","We don't need to get involved in this. At least not yet."],["???","Whatever trouble the thieves cause—real damage or public backlash—it'll all land on the current governor and the bureaucrats in power."],["???","Rosemary's use of mercenaries to fill the military's role is what led to this disaster... This is our leverage in the court of public opinion."],["???","I won't have your little side operation getting in the way of a counterattack military command has spent years preparing."],["Wyatt","I didn't say I wanted to hinder your actions... I just don't wanna go in blind. All I want is to find out what those guys are up to."],["Wyatt","Yevgeny Goman is almost certainly behind this, and I don't believe for a second that you trust him."],["???","Goman should not be underestimated... but your investigative actions are too dangerous."],["???","Since you were able to find out this much, the GSA must have known long ago. Their lack of action indicates this might be a trap set for us."],["???","You're not a fool, Morgan. But you've been away from the political arena too long... You may not understand how the winds have shifted back home."],["???","The tide has turned, Morgan. Twenty years of patience cannot be wasted... What you really need to do is withdraw from DL territory immediately, hide your Fenrisúlfr, and stay out of this."],["???","I don't want to see your name on an impeachment list."],["Wyatt","......"],["","The cowboy lies in the cockpit, letting out a long sigh."],["","On a small monitor in the upper-right corner, mercenaries in unmarked machines use the cover of dusk to move several objects glowing electric blue."],["","It's the most advanced arashi matter scanner in existence, custom-fitted to Fenrisúlfr. Its detection and imaging are precise enough to see the faintest flows through an enemy ST's arashi matter transmission framework."],["","STs equipped with this instrument can easily lock onto an enemy ST's weak points, tearing into their prey like a dire wolf."],["","After a long silence, the cowboy gives his final answer."],["Wyatt","Understood. I'll cooperate. I'm pulling out of Dawnstar League territory immediately."],["","Wyatt fires up the engine. Fenrisúlfr lunges straight at the mercenary squad like a demon out of hell."]],"468341301":[["","The heavy mine elevator slams to a halt with a metallic clang, sending a huge echo through the shaft."],["","After taking a second or two to steady herself, Mirestomp deftly removes Ludwig's blindfold."],["Mirestomp","Here."],["Ludwig","*cough... cough, cough...* Where are we...?"],["","Blinding white mine lamps make it impossible for him to keep his eyes open."],["","Then comes the smoke, dust, and an untimely smell of machine oil and disinfectant."],["Ludwig","Le... Leviathan—!?"],["","It was over, he thought. The nightmare had finally caught up with him. Not dying in that accident back then had truly been his life's worst misfortune."],["","The rust-covered Vulcan Frame slides along the old mine cart tracks."],["","Massive sections of the Mobile Fortress are pieced together as hoists rise and fall..."],["","And in the hollow center of this mine, the massive Leviathan remains lie sprawled on the ground like a wounded beast, receiving treatment from outsiders."],["Heinz","Sorry to keep you waiting, Professor Ludwig. I hope you'll forgive the late rescue. I only got out of prison myself not long ago."],["","Heinz steps from the shadows and offers Ludwig his mechanical hand."],["Ludwig","So... it was you."],["","Ludwig doesn't move. He just stares into Heinz's mocking eye, his expression ice-cold."],["Heinz","The arm you gave me hasn't been working smoothly lately. I think some of the arashi components might be aging. I'll need you to take a look."],["","When Ludwig doesn't take his hand, Heinz casually sets the mechanical arm spinning."],["","Mechanical tendons flex and shift, occasionally exposing the gun barrel hidden at the arm's core."],["Ludwig","If you're going to kill me, get it over with... I'm not working with you again."],["","Ludwig's voice is firm, but Heinz only gives a quiet snort."],["Heinz","You've got it wrong, Professor. We're not asking you to work with us... We want to help you finish what you started."],["Ludwig","I haven't left anything unfinished."],["Heinz","Really? So you've forgotten everyone from Project 1099 already... They'd be heartbroken to hear that."],["","1099... The number makes Ludwig's heart sink. A dark suspicion slowly crawls into its place."],["Ludwig","Stop beating around the bush... What are you getting at?"],["","\"Click-clack,\" Heinz's mechanical hand finally seems to settle back into smooth motion."],["","He walks over and gently pats Ludwig on the shoulder with it."],["Heinz","Patience... Before we begin, why don't you take a look at the gift I've prepared for you?"],["","On the battlefield, Skysweep's ST lies dismantled. The external cables mounted on Fenrisúlfr are linked to the interface of the defeated ST, racing against time to read the disk."],["","And not far off, the back cabin cut by the chainsaw sits exposed to the dusk sunlight, revealing the human brain wetware implanted in the frame core."],["Wyatt","The PAMS System... So Goman's plan is to smuggle DL tech into Ovett?"],["","He once saw reports about this arashium technology in the GSA database, but this is the first time he's seen it in person."],["Skysweep","Looks like the NDF sent one of its real monsters..."],["","Skysweep lies inside the carved-open wreckage, half his clothes soaked in blood, yet still smiling."],["Wyatt","So you even dug up my background? Your moles don't play around, do they?"],["Wyatt","You don't seem too worried about staying alive... But give me enough information, and maybe I'll offer you a way out."],["Skysweep","Heh... Our lives aren't worth much, boss. Throwing away yours to save us? Now that'd be a terrible deal."],["","Skysweep keeps smiling as bloody foam spills from his mouth."],["","Since becoming a mercenary, he's never been hurt this badly... Then again, he's always been the first one to run."],["","He never expected to die here—at coordinates confirmed to be completely secure—cut down by a lone NDF soldier charging in on his own."],["","Really... How can that Ovettian woman, after working for the UNCS for so long, still hold onto the dream of restoring her country?"],["","But why can't those fools see it?"],["","Wyatt catches the warning beneath the mercenary's words. Skysweep is telling him to stay out of the UNCS's internal power struggle."],["","But from the moment he decided to defy orders, there was no turning back for him."],["Wyatt","It's her, isn't it...? Natalia Coronado. Madam's favorite \"daughter.\""],["Skysweep","Heh, you're sharp... I thought I was the only one here who wasn't an idiot... *cough, cough*"],["","But what good does knowing the answer do? They're both just pawns in someone else's hands."],["","Even this act of going rogue was probably anticipated, mapped out on the chessboard long ago..."],["Wyatt","Alright. I'd better be going before your friends arrive."],["","The data transfer completes. Fenrisúlfr retracts its cables and rises from Skysweep's ruined ST."],["","Fenrisúlfr plucks the abandoned PAMS System from the wreckage like a ripe peach fallen from a tree."],["Skysweep","Guess this is goodbye... Honestly, I still think you're better suited to mercenary work."],["Wyatt","So do I... But sometimes you've got to do things you aren't suited for—and aren't any good at."],["Skysweep","Haha, you like doing things the hard way, huh?"],["Wyatt","It's the only way I know."],["Ludwig","You... You bastards! What have you done to everyone—?!"],["Liliya","Don't start playing the hero just yet, newcomer... More than half of them volunteered to give their lives for science."],["Liliya","At least, that's what your superior told me."],["","Deep inside the mine, row after row of sealed wetware cultivation pods stand neatly arranged throughout a makeshift laboratory."],["","The various instruments connecting the pods betray this room's true nature: it is a large matrix built from dozens of PAMS Systems, all linked to the Leviathan at the center of the mine."],["","And on the screen below the matrix equipment, a list of \"donor\" personnel is displayed, each name vividly remembered by Ludwig."],["","They're all people he once knew—victims who died in the Leviathan rampage long ago."],["","Yet now, they stand before Ludwig again in an entirely different form."],["Heinz","I imagine you've already met your old colleagues?"],["Heinz","Since we're already accomplices, I'll cut to the chase."],["","Heinz's voice comes through the headset, as he stands on a nearby overpass, watching the collapse of the former project leader."],["Heinz","To make amends for the mistakes we made, we've done all we can to rescue those who were affected."],["Heinz","Unfortunately, not everyone survived that disaster..."],["Heinz","For those conventional treatment couldn't save, we had no choice but to take more... regrettable measures."],["","No, this is enslavement. Being incorporated into the PAMS System means completely losing one's free will, existing only as a tool to be manipulated."],["","The Dawnstar League uses the \"souls\" of thousands of fallen heroes to maintain several elite forces—and keep West Milkhama in check."],["Ludwig","Turning them into these... things. This is how you make amends?"],["Heinz","But it's your fault, Ludwig... Your jealousy led to this disaster..."],["Ludwig","No... I didn't..."],["Heinz","You didn't just kill Lucas. You killed everyone standing before you."],["Ludwig","——"],["","The truth lodges in Ludwig's throat like a bone. No amount of denial can change what he already knows deep down."],["","The guilt he once tried to escape through death finally catches up and closes around his throat again..."],["Liliya","If you really can't bear to part with your companions, it's actually quite simple."],["Liliya","Before this wetware's shipped to Ovett, if you can successfully reset that Leviathan, there might be room for negotiation with Goman and the others."]],"468345101":[["","Fourteen years ago..."],["Lucas","Wow! The department's vacation request has been approved. Starting tomorrow, we can finally take a break!"],["","Cheers erupt throughout the Project 1099 research facility, sweeping away months of tension and gloom."],["Vitt","Finally... No more work? I feel like I'm about to fall apart..."],["Linda","Book the ferry tickets! Come on, book them!"],["Lisa","We've only got two days off. You're seriously going away for just two days?"],["Linda","It's special leave! No surveillance, no rotting away inside the compound—of course I'm going out to kick back and unwind!"],["Linda","Oh, right! I heard the nature reserve on Minet Island just opened. Don't you want to check it out?"],["Lars","Check out what? The whales contaminated by arashi matter? I heard they swim like this... and this..."],["Linda","Stop making that face, Lars... It's disgusting. Lisa, are you really not coming? We can get discounted tickets for two!"],["Lisa","I do want to go, but somehow Milkhama's become the latest tourist hotspot. Everywhere's packed. It's such a pain..."],["Lisa","I don't get it. It's a run-down island in the middle of nowhere. How did it suddenly become popular?"],["Linda","The war's over. \"Post-war reconstruction\" is a gold mine for the corporate sharks."],["Vitt","Sigh, when will a big business opportunity fall into our laps...? The arashi matter transmission project has such potential... why hasn't anyone recognized its value and invested in us?!"],["Lucas","Ludwig, why are you still staring at that screen? Our leave starts tomorrow..."],["Ludwig","Hmm..."],["Lucas","Why don't we all go out for dinner tonight? It's been ages since we've gone anywhere together!"],["Ludwig","Hmm..."],["Lucas","Ludwig? What are you even looking at...?"],["","Lucas gets up and walks behind Ludwig. Ludwig hurriedly closes the email on his screen."],["Ludwig","Why are you hovering over me...? Go to dinner without me. Someone has to stay behind and keep watch."],["Lucas","But... wait a minute, was that an email from the DLAF?"],["Ludwig","Yes... it was them. Is that a problem?"],["Lucas","I'm just curious why they'd contact you... Oh, it's that officer Heinz, right?! He tried our product, didn't he? Did he get back to us?"],["Ludwig","He... well, he said his prosthetic is in good condition, so he might consider continuing to cooperate with us."],["Lucas","That's great! If we can establish a connection with the DLAF, then—"],["Vitt","Hey! Lud, we're going out for dinner, you coming!?"],["Lars","Anyway, whether he comes or not, he'll foot the bill in the end... You're on intercept duty, Lucas! Only let him in after we've finished ordering everything we want!"],["Lucas","You guys are unbelievable..."],["Linda","Hurry up, hurry up—last one to arrive has to grill the meat for everyone!"],["","If we had just continued along that old path..."],["","Perhaps everything could've been so different..."],["","I'm sorry, everyone... In the end, I..."],["","*BOOM——*"],["","A tremendous blast of air erupts, shaking loose dirt and grit throughout the mine—"],["Liliya","Leviathan... has really activated!?"],["","At the center of the mine, the long-dormant Leviathan awakens with a roar."],["","The massive Vulcan frame drags new armor sections into position, completing the final stage of reconstruction..."],["Liliya","Losing to an old relic like this stings... But whatever. It's nearly ready for the grave anyway. Might as well squeeze some value out of it first."],["","Liliya looks at the gaunt figure before the console. He seems ready to collapse in the slightest breeze."],["Heinz","As expected of you, Ludwig. Every time I think I've seen your limit, you surprise me again."],["Heinz","Keep working with us, and both our futures will become far more interesting."],["Ludwig","I did it... Now it's your turn to fulfill your promise."],["","He looks up with bloodshot eyes."],["Heinz","Rest assured, I won't go back on our trade..."],["Heinz","But before I had over the PAMS System wetware, there's still one final step."],["Ludwig","What else do you want?!"],["","Ludwig glares at Heinz, his right hand slowly moving toward the lever beside the console."],["","This is his last resort—to go down with Heinz. If Heinz were to break his promise, he would immediately pull down the lever and force Leviathan to shut down mid-activation."],["","The ancient engine would overload in both directions and explode. At the very least, Leviathan would be crippled beyond repair..."],["","However, at this moment, he finds his hand trembling uncontrollably."],["Heinz","If you pull that lever, everything will have been for naught, you know?"],["","Heinz watches Ludwig's hand reaching for the lever and gives a gentle smile."],["Heinz","After putting in so much effort to return to Project 1099, even if it meant becoming wetware just to see their dream through..."],["Heinz","To fall just when the break of day was in sight... Your companions must have felt such bitter regret."],["Ludwig","You're saying..."],["Heinz","Everyone in Project 1099 voluntarily signed donation forms and willingly became testees of the PAMS System..."],["","Heinz's prosthetic eye opens, projecting the full Project 1099 integration plan and the researchers' brain-donation agreements across the battered console."],["Ludwig","You... Are you joking? How could everyone—"],["","Before Ludwig can react, a sharp pain pierces the back of his neck."],["","He spins around, but all he sees is Liliya's blurred outline."],["Liliya","What a pain... I do feel sorry for you, but you'll have to take a little nap."],["Liliya","Hurry up. Goman's getting impatient."],["Heinz","Understood... Now, let Milkhama witness our vengeance!"],["Wyatt","Calling Sunset Valley... Calling Sunset Valley..."],["Wyatt","Heh, just as I thought... Have all the outbound channels really been cut off...?"],["","A massive gust of wind pressure emanates from the giant object flying overhead, flattening the vegetation along the mountainside."],["","Wyatt sighs softly, using a sensor probe to capture the Leviathan's trail while doing everything he can to keep his ST hidden."],["","By tracking the Thunderbolt Squad, he finally locates the abandoned mine hidden inside the mountain—their base of operations."],["","But what waits for him is a Mobile Fortress rising from the ancient mine... and a signal that dies immediately."],["Wyatt","If I had known this thing was waiting for me, I would have listened to that old man and gone home..."],["","Now he really is stuck, though he probably wouldn't have gone this far without someone deliberately leading him here."],["Wyatt","So what now? Do I have my ST put its hands up and surrender, or pretend I saw nothing and keep walking into the mine?"],["","Wyatt directs the question at a comm line filled with nothing but a busy tone."],["","At the mountain's summit, a sniper ST quietly releases its lock."],["","If we hurry now, it shouldn't be too late."],["Wyatt","Those guys actually let you stand guard... What a waste of talent."],["","For all our sakes, I've got no choice but to take this gamble..."],["","Leviathan's former chief researcher is down there. He should know how to stop it."],["","Watch yourself, cowboy."]],"468345301":[["Liliya","You... how did you get down here!?"],["","The intruding ST moves like a ghost, tearing through the defensive perimeter. Even the trap-lined route fails to slow it down."],["","Most of the stronghold's forces have already followed Leviathan to the main battlefield. An enemy appearing here without warning can only mean the outer sentries have fallen..."],["Liliya","Hey... Natalia? Natalia!"],["","......"],["","Only a dead tone answers."],["Liliya","Tch... You win, I surrender, I surrender!"],["","Liliya tosses down her weapon and opens the cockpit. The intruder doesn't lower his guard."],["Wyatt","You're the Leviathan researcher...?"],["Liliya","Yes, that's me!"],["","Liliya decisively responds to the visitor's question. She has already determined that as long as the opponent remains hidden in his ST, she has no chance of winning."],["","But if she can lure him out, one of her syringes might end the fight."],["","Upon hearing Liliya's response, her opponent doesn't say a word. He answers instead with his chainsaw, its blade roaring to life. Startled, Liliya loses her footing and tumbles to the ground..."],["Liliya","What... what are you doing!? I said I surrender—I surrender!"],["Wyatt","Don't play tricks on me, little girl. My intel said nothing about the researcher being a dame..."],["Liliya","Hmm..."],["","Even this kind of information got leaked... But who leaked the intel? Was it that woman, or those unreliable mercenaries?"],["Wyatt","So where's the researcher? Or maybe you know how to stop that thing too?"],["Liliya","I don't know where that researcher is..."],["Liliya","But I do know how to stop the Leviathan."],["","The Leviathan... can no longer be stopped."],["","The question receives two completely opposite answers simultaneously. Wyatt opens the locator and quickly locks onto the figure bound in the corner of the console."],["Wyatt","Looks like I've found my man."],["Ludwig","I suppose so, but you showed up too late."],["Ludwig","Once the Leviathan is activated, it cannot be stopped. This has been a flaw that has never been overcome."],["","He sits alone in the corner with his head down, his voice cold and low."],["","He's probably telling the truth. In the few minutes since entering the mine, Wyatt has already read Natalia's report on Leviathan."],["","During the Milthus incident, the berserk Leviathan was ultimately taken out by a strong electromagnetic weapon that had been positioned beforehand, punching through the arashi matter matrix in its armor."],["","But this latest attack was far more sudden. Wyatt has no doubt the NDF can destroy the Leviathan, but doing so will only worsen the already volatile situation between East and West Milkhama. A border clash could quickly become something much bigger..."],["","In fact, this was probably Goman's real intention."],["Wyatt","Really... is there no way?"],["Ludwig","......"],["","Cold silence is his only answer. Then, as Wyatt hesitates, the sharp click of a weapon being cocked rings through the chamber."],["Liliya","He's lying, you know!"],["","Liliya beams at Fenrisúlfr, an oversized syringe gun in her hands and aimed straight at the bound Ludwig."],["Liliya","He's lying. He knows how to stop the Leviathan—he just doesn't want to say. To him, the lives of the UNCS are a fair price to pay to recover his old colleagues—even if all that's left of them is their brains."],["Ludwig","You—!?"],["","Ludwig turns sharply, snapping his eyes toward Liliya. But between the two, a massive chainsaw blocks the line of fire."],["","His reaction says it all."],["Wyatt","Go on, girl... I think I have enough leverage to negotiate with you."],["Liliya","Think about it, old man... Leviathan was smashed to pieces in Milthus. There's no way it's still as strong as it used to be."],["Liliya","And you've seen what we're working with down here. The only assembly rig we have was stolen from a ruined NDF fortress..."],["Wyatt","So?"],["Liliya","So..."],["","Liliya twirls the syringe gun and points it toward the enormous black curtain behind the console."],["Liliya","The arashium core of Leviathan has long been severely damaged, and its current operation relies entirely on the powerful computational support provided by the PAMS System..."],["Liliya","So, with the connection between the PAMS System and Leviathan is severed, that flying monster becomes nothing but a paper tiger—a massive, helpless target floating in the sky."],["Liliya","As for the price..."],["Ludwig","Shut up!"],["","Ludwig roars at Liliya, yet his wrath is blocked by Wyatt, who stands between them."],["Wyatt","Cut the connection... The brain wetware will die, right?"],["Liliya","You've done your homework... Because the command to unilaterally disconnect from the console is locked, to stop Leviathan, a more... violent method is required."],["","Liliya glances at the PAMS brain matrix hidden behind the curtain, then at the chainsaw blocking her path. She clenches her teeth in excitement."],["Ludwig","Don't believe her! She's lying! Don't listen to her!"],["","Ludwig continues to struggle. His frantic shouting only makes his guilt more obvious, but he has no other choice."],["","If he waits for Leviathan to be shot down, he can activate the life-support systems the instant the connection breaks. There might still be a chance to save them."],["","Project 1099 was founded to use the properties of arashi matter to create a new generation of prosthetics—stronger, more precise, and with almost no delay..."],["","As long as everyone is still here, there's still hope. As long as they're alive, there's still a chance to put everything right."],["","Then he can finally make up for what he did. All these wasted years will finally mean something..."],["","Even if it's only a lie he tells himself, an illusion spun to keep himself moving, Ludwig has to—"],["Liliya","You're quite decisive. I've heard that the UNCS has a tradition of recruiting arashi matter researchers..."],["","The blade of the chainsaw begins to spin again—Wyatt has already made his choice."],["Liliya","Have you considered applying to your boss for funding to open a private laboratory on this island?"],["Ludwig","No! Please, no—!!!"],["","But only the blade moves. Fenrisúlfr holds its position without striking."],["","Wyatt looks at the arashi matter detector, which shows no response, and says with a hint of confusion."],["Wyatt","But behind this curtain..."],["","The chainsaw suddenly surges forward and shreds the curtain concealing the Project 1099 PAMS wetware."],["Wyatt","There's nothing here?"],["","Leviathan tears through the sky, looking down upon the distant UNCS territory. Below, countless lights shine across the land, proof of the prosperity built in the twenty years since the war."],["","It is somewhat regrettable."],["","After all this time waiting, his plan is finally coming to fruition. And it seems even he is not immune to the creeping panic of running late."],["Yevgeny","You're off course, Heinz! What are you doing?! Rayneburg is the other way!"],["Yevgeny","Heinz—"],["Heinz","Relax, Goman. I'm just taking a little detour to avenge you..."],["Heinz","Look at the NDF Marine Battalion in Sunset Valley. Our sudden approach has thrown the whole base into chaos."],["Heinz","And all those machines hidden below? Perfect hosts for parasitism."],["Yevgeny","You..."],["Yevgeny","Have Liliya check—"],["","The comm suddenly goes dead. Heinz has been kicked from the channel, leaving only the thunder of Leviathan's engines inside the chamber."],["","It doesn't matter anymore... A scarred lone wolf with no pack eventually learns to make adversity its companion."],["","And once it finds its prey, biting down is only natural."],["","Crashing the Leviathan into the governor's mansion in Rayneburg? What a wasteful, ridiculous plan. A perfect monument to the stupidity of those restorationists..."],["Heinz","...Clearly, neither power nor force is in their hands, yet they vainly imagine themselves as the arbiter of war."],["","Heinz's chuckle echoes through the chamber. He glances at the launch bays standing ready. Packed with PAMS wetware, they'll become the foundation of an army that belongs to him alone."],["","They'll be absolutely loyal. Ovett's imprinting technology will turn them into perfect weapons of war."],["","From this moment on, he will never again be a pawn of the great powers—or Obsidian."],["UNCS Soldier","Sir, the enemy forces approaching Rayneburg have suddenly withdrawn. The flying Mobile Fortress appears to be heading toward Sunset Valley..."],["","Air-raid sirens howl as the NDF builds layer upon layer of defenses outside Rayneburg. But the enemy, already poised to attack, suddenly pulls back instead."],["","The UNCS officer responsible for organizing defense nervously watches the tactical screen, as strings of intel and comms are relayed back and forth in the command room."],["UNCS Captain","Sir, the DLAF continues to deny any involvement, but intelligence comparisons confirm that the airship-type Mobile Fortress is Leviathan—a weapon developed and built by the Dawnstar League!"],["Shin Sagara","That thing... it's back?"],["","Shin Sagara stares coldly at the screen as wave after wave of interceptor missiles bursts uselessly against Leviathan's defensive matrix."],["","Consistent with the previous intel from the battle against Milthus, conventional weapons struggle to inflict damage on this flying monster."],["","However, the high-energy electromagnetic weapons that have been proven effective have yet to be deployed at the designated positions."],["","The military higher-ups have shelved the ground combat unit's request for the deployment of high-energy electromagnetic weapons, which means the authority for the power support system cannot be delegated... And without power support, even if the rail gun is set up, it'll be a sitting duck."],["","The old-timers are stalling. They're gambling against Rosemary, looking to settle the score after the military faction spent more than a year sidelined in Milkhama."],["","And the price of that gamble will be an attack on the governor's office—and the lives of the soldiers on the front line. Then military command will have all the justification it needs to march in and seize control of Milkhama."],["Shin Sagara","What about the GSA, how have they responded?"],["UNCS Captain","The GSA contacted us over a secure line. They said they would use technical means to approve the program and permissions, and asked us to set up the rail gun first."],["UNCS Captain","But if the enemy abandons the attack on Rayneburg and instead targets the Marine Camp... even GSA support will not be enough."],["","Shin Sagara's brow furrows—a rare sight. Throughout his military career, composure and ruthlessness have defined him. No enemy, however powerful, has ever shaken him."],["","However, he is powerless against the shadows behind his own lines."],["Shin Sagara","Well, since they all want to gamble... we can only take a chance too."],["Shin Sagara","Leave only the outermost defensive line at Rayneburg! All other forces are to redeploy to the Sunset Valley Marine Battalion immediately!"],["UNCS Captain","But sir... That leaves the capital exposed. If the DLAF seizes the opportunity—"],["Shin Sagara","Whoever's coming isn't the DLAF. And even if it is, we couldn't stop them alone anyway."],["","After a moment of thought, Shin Sagara makes his decision."],["UNCS Captain","But we still don't have authorization to deploy the high-energy weapons at the Marine Battalion..."],["","Then we'll have to hope the higher-ups come to their senses in time."],["","Shin Sagara doesn't say a word aloud. He gathers his gear and strides out of the command room."],["UNCS Soldier","Secure line comms incoming, sir! It's Lieutenant Colonel Wyatt Morgan..."],["UNCS Soldier","He said... he has a way to stop the Leviathan!"]],"468349101":[["Lucas","Why... Why didn't you tell me the truth? Didn't you trust me?"],["Lucas","We never had to go down this road. We had other choices!"],["Linda","So... we're part of the military now, right?"],["Linda","I'd be saying goodbye to my free time... But if Lisa and the others are here, it wouldn't be too bad."],["Vitt","To be honest, I'm a bit uneasy because I've experienced war firsthand. I know what those DLAF guys are really like..."],["Vitt","But this is Milkhama—not like we have much choice... Well, it is what it is."],["Lars","Oh, the army... Those guys at the special research institute, the way they strut around it's all like this... and like that..."],["Lars","Like this... like that... Wait, are we going to have to strut around like that too?"],["","I understand your remorse, but you could've stopped that rampage incident, couldn't you?"],["","Why didn't you? Was it jealousy? Did you use a staged accident to get rid of your greatest rival...?"],["","You've become just like them. Do you hate yourself for it?"],["","There's still one way to stop Leviathan."],["Wyatt","You know a way? Are you serious?"],["","Yes. The same choice he made back then..."],["Lisa","No... Leviathan's outer restraining armor is about to collapse. There's no hope left for us..."],["Lucas","No, there is still a way. Reconnect the direct line, and I'll stop Leviathan!"],["","Reconnect the direct line, and I'll stop Leviathan."],["Liliya","You're lying. I've read the Leviathan development files Heinz gave me... The neural encryption key exists only inside Lucas Bonat, the project's chief researcher."],["Liliya","He's dead. No one can hack into Leviathan's arashi matter core from outside anymore, which means no one can seize control."],["","No, I also have a copy of that neural encryption."],["","And I... That's why I..."],["Heinz","Do you see? Do you see how terrifying human jealousy can be? However, I don't consider it to be something shameful, rather, it may very well become our common ground."],["Heinz","Whether intentional or not, the fact remains that you adjusted the restraining device the day before the incident without authorization..."],["Heinz","However, I have erased all evidence of your crimes."],["Heinz","The true cause of this accident was not the failure of Leviathan's restraining device, nor your \"deliberate sabotage,\" but rather the blind ambition and misfortune of your genius friend..."],["Heinz","In the end, the UNCS spy, Lucas Bonat, met his demise due to his crimes in the incident involving the out-of-control Mobile Fortress..."],["","Although I never meant for him to die..."],["","But when the accident happened, I didn't use my permissions to stop it."],["Ludwig","Are you... are you crazy!? Doing this will only get you killed!"],["Lucas","It's alright. I've never cared that much about living or dying... I led the development of this ST's arashi matter core. All I'm doing is uploading my consciousness and becoming Leviathan's administrator."],["Lucas","My only regret is that I may never see you all like this again. Take care of yourselves."],["Lucas","Goodbye."],["","Now it's my turn."],["","I may never see you all like this again... Take care of yourselves."],["","Goodbye."],["Wyatt","You're awake. Sleep well? You've got a big job ahead of you."],["Ludwig","Not bad, though my dreams were all over the place..."],["Ludwig","I suppose this is goodbye."],["","Fenrisúlfr races toward the NDF Marine Battalion with Wyatt and Ludwig aboard."],["","Not far away, the colossal Leviathan cuts through the golden light of dawn, closing in on its final destination."],["Wyatt","The NDF should have everything you asked for ready."],["Wyatt","STs equipped with the Dive system, high-powered jetpacks... Thanks to both side's prep, all this high-end gear is ours for the taking."],["Ludwig","Thank you."],["","Silence settles over the cramped cockpit again. Wyatt considers offering a few words of encouragement—or calling Ludwig a hero—but says nothing."],["","Ludwig has already told him the price of stopping Leviathan. Wyatt knows these may be the last peaceful moments of the man's life."],["","He doesn't want to disturb him. So they travel the final stretch in silence, like condemned men riding toward the gallows with nothing left to do but stare out the window."],["Ludwig","Is this... what West Milkhama has become?"],["","Ludwig looks through the passenger module's viewport at the UNCS towns still sleeping beneath the last shadows before dawn."],["","Towering buildings and sweeping elevated highways interlock in patterns he's never seen before, weaving a vision of prosperity."],["Wyatt","You haven't been over here in a long time, have you? Makes sense. You spent all those years in a laboratory, then the rest locked in a cell."],["Wyatt","Honestly, I was stunned too when I came back to the island."],["Wyatt","When I left, this was nothing but barren sand and shell craters... Blink once, and it looks like this."],["Wyatt","If the new gold rush was Milkhama's golden age... then I suppose these last twenty years have been its gilded age."],["Ludwig","Gilded... age..."],["","Ludwig murmurs the words as light and shadow drift across his eyes."],["","He sees clouds scattered like dust from a sieve. Beneath them, the distant Mouty Mountains rise like the backs of cattle and sheep, rolling gently across the horizon. They remind him of the smell of grass on the pastures of his childhood."],["","He remembers arriving on Milkhama with Lucas after endless days and nights adrift at sea. Nothing else in his life ever matches the joy of seeing the island's skyline for the first time."],["","He remembers the fish Lars and Lisa kept in the laboratory. The faces they pulled against the glass. The trails of bubbles left behind as the frightened fish scattered."],["","He sees towers rising from the earth and countless lights threading together across elevated roads and columns of STs."],["","He sees arashi mines flare to life and die away, ships drifting in and out of port, and dreamers chasing impossible ambitions. He sees everyone who was still alive back then raising their glasses together..."],["","The memories fade. The two race onward without a word, the cockpit filled with everything they cannot say."],["UNCS Soldier","Next volley! Interception weapons... fire!"],["UNCS Captain","Is it not working... Colonel! The current anti-air weapons are ineffective against the target! We're barely able to hold our positions!"],["UNCS Captain","Not to mention whatever mystery projectile that monster just threw at us..."],["","Gliding into the fray, a black mechanical orb floats above the battlefield, deflecting all incoming gunfire. The interference field radiating around it leaves even state-of-the-art tracking missiles flying blind, slamming into each other like headless flies."],["","Cable-like limbs extend from behind the spheres like the tentacles of deep-sea creatures, lashing toward the command STs below."],["Shin Sagara","A hacking weapon—!?"],["","Standard STs collapse one after another as screams flood the comms. Only a handful of elite pilots who have activated Dive can resist the unpredictable parasitism."],["Shin Sagara","How much longer until the electromagnetic weapon is ready?!"],["UNCS Captain","We're still trying to secure emergency power..."],["Shin Sagara","Given the situation... let the Falcon Force hold the line for now."],["Wyatt","Looks like I missed the party..."],["","Amidst the rising dust, Fenrisúlfr charges forward. The sheer wear on its foot-rollers tells the story: even top-of-the-line armor plating couldn't survive a high-speed trek of this length unscathed."],["Shin Sagara","Whether you're coming or not, I'm setting up our defenses."],["Wyatt","Well, my assistant made it clear—wearing down the Leviathan's defenses is a job only you guys can pull off."],["Wyatt","And he can only lend a hand at the last second."],["","Wyatt shares Fenrisúlfr's Arashi matter imaging with every NDF unit on the battlefield. Across Leviathan's surface, its adaptive matrix constantly shifts to intercept attacks from every direction."],["Shin Sagara","Since you're here, enter the formation. Quick—we don't have time to waste."]],"468349301":[["UNCS Soldier","Officer, there's a gap in the protection matrix at the bottom of the Leviathan! But... we've lost a lot of men!"],["Shin Sagara","The rail gun's still not in position?!"],["UNCS Captain","The GSA bypassed approval and directly granted permissions, but... the power supply... it definitely won't make it in time..."],["Shin Sagara","Then we have no choice! Maintain saturation fire! Wyatt—!"],["Shin Sagara","We're counting on you..."],["Wyatt","Don't look at me. Look at him!"],["Wyatt","Hey. You ready?"],["","Ludwig sits inside the cramped cockpit, his frail back covered in neural electrodes. Powerful painkillers and neural stimulants flow into his bloodstream through additional needles..."],["","Dive isn't even active yet. He can barely breathe. His heart rate and neural load are already at their limits. With an ordinary body like his, activating Dive may destroy him instantly."],["Ludwig","Huff... huff... so this... is the Nova Frame..."],["","A faint sting of defeat rises within him. Even now, at the final moment he has long prepared for, the pride carved into his bones refuses to stay quiet."],["Ludwig","But... it's still far from our masterpiece, right, Lucas?"],["","He slams the ready button. The light strips across the ST go dark in unison, while the booster frame below erupts with a deafening roar."],["","The moment the signal goes out, the UNCS forces waiting above clear a wide space. A rising platform carries Ludwig's ST to the surface."],["Wyatt","Ready to Launch!"],["","Leviathan immediately detects the movement below. Missiles and torrents of flame descend upon the waiting ST."],["","Interceptor fire collides with the incoming missiles, filling the sky with blossoms of flame."],["Heinz","Ha, what kind of trick is this? Another one of those suicidal stunts your UNCS is so famous for? This isn't twenty years ago..."],["Wyatt","It seems those tactics from twenty years ago left an impression. Haven't moved on, huh?"],["Wyatt","Professor, the authorization has been transferred to you. Go—now!"],["Ludwig","I... hear you loud and clear!"],["Lucas","It's alright. I've never cared that much about living or dying... I led the development of this ST's arashi matter core. All I'm doing is uploading my consciousness and becoming Leviathan's administrator."],["Lucas","My only regret is that I may never see you all like this again. Take care of yourselves."],["","Like my dearest friends before me, I go to my death protecting the dream we once shared."],["","There's no better ending than this."],["","Fire erupts from the boosters. Ludwig's ST launches toward Leviathan without hesitation, streaking through the sky like a flash of light."],["Heinz","You're...!?"],["","Ughhhhhhhhhhh—!"],["","Blood pours from his ears, the metallic tang of crimson rising in his throat. Vision blinded by red, his body reduced to raw agony... As his physical senses slip away, a newfound awareness surges outward at a terrifying speed."],["","The Dive of the Nova-Frame has been initiated, and the α Matter Matrix, originally meant for protection, resonates with the unexpected intruder."],["Heinz","Of all times... now you decide to play the hero."],["","Heinz gives a cold snort. He really had considered sparing his former accomplice—letting him avoid becoming fuel for the Hard Reset Plan."],["","And yet, some people always insist on doing things the hard way."],["","Heinz grips the controls for Leviathan's ventral guns and opens fire on Ludwig's ST."],["","The barrage flashes like a wall of blinding light. Already buckling under the strain of its high-speed ascent, the ST is torn through by autocannon fire."],["","Blood, oil, and blue-glowing liquid Arashi matter spray from the bullet holes. Metal shards and sparks peel away like splinters, tracing falling arcs through the wind."],["","At this point, he can't even feel the pain. His nervous system has burned out completely. All that remains are a few faint chemical signals inside his brain..."],["","——"],["","I... still couldn't..."],["","His link with Leviathan is severed in an instant. All that remains is the endless sensation of falling."],["","He can't think. He can't speak. His vision turns pure white, as though he's sinking into a boundless white sea."],["","He spent his entire life exploring the boundary between neural signals and the human body, trying to steal nature's power to create life and grant arashi matter the ability to unite metal and flesh."],["","He once questioned the truth of soul and memory, researching the sustainability of consciousness in arashi with his close friends to avoid the inevitable end of all things."],["","It's over."],["","Yet in this infinite descent..."],["","He felt a hand."],["","Suddenly, it grabbed him."],["Lucas","You finally came, Ludwig."],["Lucas","Everyone has been waiting for you for a long time."],["Lucas","Remember? The last one here has to grill the meat for everyone!"],["Heinz","Hmph..."],["","Flames swallow Ludwig's ST. Under the concentrated barrage, it breaks apart in seconds."],["","The threat warning disappears. The breach Ludwig opened seals immediately, and Leviathan becomes untouchable once more."],["","And with that... it comes to an end."],["","Heinz leans back in the pilot's seat and watches the NDF lines retreat below. For a moment, he sees the East Coast front twenty years ago, collapsing beneath the NDF's assault."],["","But the man he once wanted revenge on is already gone. Now that victory is finally his, it feels strangely hollow."],["Heinz","It ends here."],["","The past crashes over him in waves. He's a sailor crawling from a shipwreck, only to find the reef he swore revenge upon has vanished beneath an endless sea."],["","All that remains is the lonely sound of the waves."],["","...Waves?"],["","Heinz jolts upright and searches for the source of the eerie sound."],["","He adjusts every channel and audio circuit he can find, but nothing shuts it out."],["","The sound surges like a flood, filling every corner of Leviathan—and every hollow place inside him."],["Heinz","Is that... the arashi matter core...?!"],["","The arashi matter matrix remains intact. The bombardment outside still can't penetrate it. Yet every component linked through the Arashi matter drive frame begins disconnecting one by one."],["","Across the central control panel, a highest-priority command appears in enormous letters: \"9901\"—Project 1099 written backward—Leviathan's self-disassembly command."],["","Heinz seizes the controls and hammers in command after command, trying to reclaim authority."],["","However, all he receives in response is error, error, error..."],["Heinz","Ludwig, you actually—!!!!!!!!!"],["","Before he can finish, the waves become a tsunami. The entire cockpit convulses, then vanishes into blinding white."],["","The engine compartment tears away from the control cabin. The ammunition bay detonates. The unlaunched PAMS wetware ejects into the sky as the fluid outer frame peels apart..."],["","It all happens in an instant—"],["Shin Sagara","Did he succeed?"],["","The entire NDF stares up in silence. Leviathan detonates in midair, trailing a long tail of flame as it falls toward the Sunset Valley desert."],["Wyatt","Get a rescue team moving now... Find him! Save him! Move!"],["","Wyatt roars over the comms. Fenrisúlfr is already racing toward the falling wreckage of Ludwig's ST."],["","His chances of survival were zero. Even without the explosion, the Nova Frame's Dive load would kill an ordinary man like Ludwig outright."],["","Deep down, Wyatt knows this. The thought won't leave his mind. His body moves anyway."],["Ludwig","Looks like there's no turning back now..."],["Ludwig","Next, the arashi matter core will completely shatter, and soon even this space will cease to exist."],["Ludwig","You probably still hate me. This was your life's work."],["Lucas","I don't really care."],["Lucas","After all, nothing lasts forever."],["Lucas","Not Leviathan. Not the Arashi matter core. Not everyone from Project 1099. Not even the age when Milkhama could build any ST imaginable around a Vulcan frame..."],["Lucas","What's past is past. Everything comes to an end, eventually."],["Ludwig","Well... maybe you're right, but that doesn't sound like something you'd say."],["Lucas","Of course it doesn't. I only captured fragments of his memories. I could never recreate his personality perfectly."],["Ludwig","What? You're...?"],["","I told you. Everything ends. The dead don't return, and you can't keep begging a dead man's ghost to answer you."],["Ludwig","You're... the consciousness born from within the Leviathan...? So he really did succeed..."],["Ludwig","It's just... a little disappointing."],["","You don't deserve to see them one last time. Someone like you should keep living—with all that guilt engraved into your being."],["","Farewell, Ludwig."],["","Carry your regret. Carry your guilt. Drag it all behind you and keep crawling forward..."],["","..."],["","A sigh slips through the howling wind. Then comes the click of a weapon being cocked."],["","Click—"],["","\"Accordion.\" You've crossed the line."],["","Stepping out from the shadows, the figure shows his face."],["","Not heading back yet?"],["","The woman turns calmly and meets Anderson's gaze. Far behind her, Leviathan breaks into countless burning fragments across the sky—a grand final firework."],["Natalia","...I didn't expect you to arrive so soon."],["Anderson","Madam isn't going to be pleased when she finds out what you've done."],["Natalia","I know. But I didn't have a choice. So what stopped you? Why didn't you pull the trigger?"],["","Natalia stares into the dark muzzle. Her hair and coat whip in the wind."],["Anderson","You never told Goman that Heinz was deceiving him... You were the first to learn that Heinz had secretly transferred the PAMS System onto Leviathan without telling the Ovettian restorationists, weren't you?"],["Anderson","If you'd warned Goman in time, the attack on Rayneburg wouldn't have fallen apart... and I discovered..."],["Anderson","There were others deliberately leaking intel to Wyatt Morgan, goading him to come and ruin this plan... So I can't confirm which side you're on."],["Natalia","So... it turns out that you are the \"Sand Whale\"? Then I really must thank you for showing mercy."],["","A hint of surprise flashes in the woman's eyes, followed by a charming smile."],["Natalia","I promised Madam. She is the one who gave me a new life, like a mother... I could never betray her..."],["Natalia","Yet the restorationists hunger for conflict more fiercely than East or West, chasing advanced technology my homeland could never produce... Playing all these sides against one another gets exhausting."],["Anderson","War in Milkhama is inevitable. You know it, I know it, and Madam knows it."],["Anderson","If this is only about settling a personal score and putting the NDF in its place, there are safer ways to do it."],["","Natalia says nothing. She simply turns back toward the horizon."],["","In the distance, Leviathan's burning fragments gradually fade. Morning light spills across the land as commuter trains wind between cities and hills beneath fresh contrails in the sky..."],["","For better or worse, another day begins in West Milkhama—just like every day of the twenty years since the war."],["","Amid the rumble of ST engines, Anderson watches Natalia turn away. Answering her silence with his own, he slowly lowers the gun and looks past her desolate silhouette toward the horizon."],["","The age of carefree singing and dancing is over. All that's left is the long, heavy night closing in."]]};
